{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"daf4a150d8f4210d349d6f6c81671e75fe5f0d67c5e86a143de9aad12741aa64","slug":"language-server-protocol","location":"/72-language-server-protocol/language-server-protocol.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Jupyter integration with the Language Server Protocol","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Nicholas Bollweg","given":"Nicholas","family":"Bollweg"},"name":"Nicholas Bollweg","github":"bollwyvl","id":"contributors-language-server-protocol-generated-uid-0"},{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Jeremy Tuloup","given":"Jeremy","family":"Tuloup"},"name":"Jeremy Tuloup","github":"jtpio","id":"contributors-language-server-protocol-generated-uid-1"},{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Michał Krassowski","given":"Michał","family":"Krassowski"},"name":"Michał Krassowski","github":"krassowski","id":"contributors-language-server-protocol-generated-uid-2"}],"date":"2021-09-23","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/blob/main/72-language-server-protocol/language-server-protocol.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/edit/main/72-language-server-protocol/language-server-protocol.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"language-server-protocol.md","url":"/enhancement-proposals/build/language-server-prot-0f1b0bbf98cdd589568d367484a101a0.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"MOhoFMszFl"}],"identifier":"summary","label":"Summary","html_id":"summary","implicit":true,"key":"aOirc1ZsSn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"jupyter(lab)-lsp","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"PSnfP2XmpK"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp","error":true,"key":"py47OvXEgW"},{"type":"text","value":" is a project bringing integration\nof language-specific IDE features (such as diagnostics, linting, autocompletion, refactoring) to the\nJupyter ecosystem by leveraging the established\n","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"XivvnhZ0ts"},{"type":"link","url":"https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language Server Protocol","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"k69DNEWdXJ"}],"urlSource":"https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/","key":"aZPzCE0oGf"},{"type":"text","value":" (LSP), with a good\noverview on the ","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"uCJXcU3hsC"},{"type":"link","url":"https://langserver.org","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"community knowledge site","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"GTlvQBdkvo"}],"urlSource":"https://langserver.org","key":"PTKkULSnUu"},{"type":"text","value":". We would like to propose its\nincorporation as an official sub-project of Project Jupyter. We feel this would benefit Jupyter\nusers through better discoverability of advanced interactive computing features, supported by the\n(LSP), but otherwise missing in a user’s Jupyter experience. While our repository currently features\na working implementation, the proposal is not tied to it (beyond a proposal for migration of the\nrepository to a Jupyter-managed GitHub organization) but rather aimed to guide the process of\nformalizing and evolving the way of integrating Jupyter with LSP in general.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"p87CXNsuzg"}],"key":"f4qnucOsqF"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motivation","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"Mok4ranLpJ"}],"identifier":"motivation","label":"Motivation","html_id":"motivation","implicit":true,"key":"hPToSNj5u6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A common criticism of the Jupyter environment (regardless of the front-end editor) and of the\nofficial Jupyter frontends (in light of recent, experimental support of feature-rich notebook\nedition under development by some of the major IDE developers) is the lack of advanced code\nassistance tooling. The proper tooling can improve code quality, validity of computation and\nincrease development speed and we therefore believe that it is a key ingredient of a good\ncomputational notebooks environment, which from the beginning aimed at improving the workflow of\nusers.","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"aTFknH9khx"}],"key":"xWeNx127km"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providing support for advanced coding assistance for each language separately is a daunting task,\nchallenging not only for volunteer-driven projects, but also for large companies. Microsoft\nrecognized the problem creating the Language Server Protocol with reference implementation in\nVSCode(TM).","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"RlgZbC54ic"}],"key":"axI2W8eZZ0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many language servers are community supported and available for free (see the community-maintained\nlist of ","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"nC2Q8P53PW"},{"type":"link","url":"https://langserver.org/","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"language servers","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"bol0h6zbRL"}],"urlSource":"https://langserver.org/","key":"Tpzaj8rWOU"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"tm0QRtaXyr"}],"key":"EswtrHhlYD"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide-level explanation","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"K6lKPRjHlb"}],"identifier":"guide-level-explanation","label":"Guide-level explanation","html_id":"guide-level-explanation","implicit":true,"key":"KQsAf7YD6Y"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Much like\n","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"PoFpKvch8G"},{"type":"link","url":"https://jupyter-client.readthedocs.io/en/stable/messaging.html","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter Kernel Messaging","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"M32DNXm2Qw"}],"urlSource":"https://jupyter-client.readthedocs.io/en/stable/messaging.html","key":"sU2UFDYdCJ"},{"type":"text","value":", LSP\nprovides a language-agnostic, JSON-compatible description for multiple clients to integrate with any\nnumber of language implementations. Unlike Kernel Messaging, the focus is on precise definition of\nthe many facets of static analysis and code transformation, with nearly four times the number of\nmessages of the Jupyter specification. We will discuss the opportunities and challenges of this\ncomplexity for users and maintainers of Jupyter Clients, Kernels, and related tools.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"vfK7b78PPg"}],"key":"tSmANZCqzS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key component of the repository,\n","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"H765xhCww0"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"@krassowski​/jupyterlab​-lsp","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"G08n4YwO9e"}],"urlSource":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp","key":"eRDsXKS9QS"},{"type":"text","value":", offers\nJupyter users an expanded subset of features described by the LSP as an extension to JupyterLab.\nThese features include refinements of existing Jupyter interactive computing features, such as\ncompletion and introspection, as well as new Jupyter features such as linting, reference linking,\nand symbol renaming. It is supported by ","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"AosJolsAct"},{"type":"link","url":"https://pypi.org/project/jupyter-lsp/","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"jupyter-lsp","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"DcjRWWMuHB"}],"urlSource":"https://pypi.org/project/jupyter-lsp/","key":"cCOUafggPO"},{"type":"text","value":", a\nLanguage Server- and Jupyter Client-agnostic extension of the Jupyter Notebook Server (for the ","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"prvCSTEZUU"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.x","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"DHWLM4Simh"},{"type":"text","value":"\nline) and Jupyter Server (for the ","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"rWqTqQxMgZ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1.x","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"VzK3UPAIpf"},{"type":"text","value":"). We will discuss the architecture and engineering process\nof maintaining these components at greater length, leveraging a good deal of the user and developer\n","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"mMRCVqM5xt"},{"type":"link","url":"https://jupyterlab-lsp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/?badge=latest","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"documentation","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"q2X6tugaZC"}],"urlSource":"https://jupyterlab-lsp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/?badge=latest","key":"sjZqpzsnmV"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"vdGwoupdGQ"}],"key":"N1U43vepUu"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference-level explanation","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"RWJfNMaryN"}],"identifier":"reference-level-explanation","label":"Reference-level explanation","html_id":"reference-level-explanation","implicit":true,"key":"VvCajcvlDF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current implementation of the LSP integration is a barely a proof of concept. We believe that a\ndifferent implementation should be developed to take the more comprehensive use cases and diversity\nof the Jupyter ecosystem into account; we created detailed proposals for improvement and refactoring\nof our code as explained later.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"EQX0xdnfNc"}],"key":"xumA36ILbS"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dealing with Jupyter notebooks complexity","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"Dst8A9ljm2"}],"identifier":"dealing-with-jupyter-notebooks-complexity","label":"Dealing with Jupyter notebooks complexity","html_id":"dealing-with-jupyter-notebooks-complexity","implicit":true,"key":"BmsVd3QrgX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following features need to be considered in the design:","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"jWs17aySOQ"}],"key":"sYUEnovNlM"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The interactive, data-driven computing paradigm provides additional convenience features on top of\nexisting languages:","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"IiVd6TpaNc"}],"key":"bMozYf6S7Q"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":95,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cell and line magics","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"drEsjamHJ8"}],"key":"gaVmZFUJxQ"}],"key":"ArYqcPsxhh"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tranclusions: “foreign” code in the document, often implemented as magics which uses a different\nlanguage or scope than the rest of the document (e.g. ","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"iJYRIs4jvW"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"%%html","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"pYJn7BbOZR"},{"type":"text","value":" magic in IPython)","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"xGZ380bfNV"}],"key":"XDFi0C7CQB"}],"key":"Bjjn0XCQcr"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"polyglot notebooks using cell metadata to define language","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"tuqURdsfC0"}],"key":"TKuN22R5qr"}],"key":"zgQXf3l3YY"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":95,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the concept of cells, including cell outputs and cell metadata (e.g. enabling LSP extensions to\nwarn users about unused empty cells, out of order execution markers, etc., as briefly discussed in\n","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"lZJL670Vtw"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp/issues/467","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"#467","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"XLcS3bxBKb"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/krassowski/jupyterlab-lsp/issues/467","data":{"kind":"issue","org":"krassowski","repo":"jupyterlab-lsp","issue_number":"467"},"internal":false,"protocol":"github","key":"J23HSxlBWh"},{"type":"text","value":")","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"oVu8TTuwfd"}],"key":"uNqpPZZ0S9"}],"key":"oyxWyyC5Dj"}],"key":"O6HHc0K6YI"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current implementation","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"e17sNNKwL4"}],"identifier":"current-implementation","label":"Current implementation","html_id":"current-implementation","implicit":true,"key":"qgoaVhOTjZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Currently:","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"key":"C17pJ5keqe"}],"key":"C9R7s2avKQ"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the notebook cells are concatenated into a single temporary (“virtual”) document on the frontend,\nwhich is then sent to the backend,","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"key":"dZ4LtBPlPp"}],"key":"Oc9DNHvgWG"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the navigation between coordinate system is performed by the frontend and is based solely on the\ntotal number of lines after concatenation","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"ZsHhpXwecO"}],"key":"yDCXHL5rvc"}],"key":"O0OwG6UWit"}],"key":"Octf9MvmDP"}],"key":"EWjaJyQI0k"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"as a workaround for some language servers requiring actual presence of the file on the filesystem\n(against the LSP spec, but common in some less advanced servers), our backend Jupyter server\nextension creates a temporary file on the file system (by default in the ","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"FU3vvXQyLN"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".virtual_documents","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"rdzG4lkTck"},{"type":"text","value":"\ndirectory); this is scheduled for deprecation,","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"nP8jgmEE0K"}],"key":"bbmB0w8qnK"}],"key":"zlC5ydMohv"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter server extension serves as:","position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"key":"q0amNZEHuU"}],"key":"HmEiL4evrX"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":110,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a transparent proxy between LSP language servers and frontend, speaking over websocket\nconnection","position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":109,"column":1}},"key":"nu37NnYLfe"}],"key":"o2k86us8Qa"}],"key":"ZADLWeN6FZ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a manager of language servers, determining whether specific LSP servers are installed and\nstarting their processes","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"key":"G7O7wI3cYb"}],"key":"SQBNA0klfd"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":113,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":113,"column":1},"end":{"line":116,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON files or declarative Python classes registered via entry points are used to define\nspecification of the LSP servers (where to look for an executable of the LSP server, for which\nlanguages/kernels given LSP server should be used, what is its display name, etc.)","position":{"start":{"line":113,"column":1},"end":{"line":113,"column":1}},"key":"PgXa4jpg3V"}],"key":"bMGQoT9E9L"}],"key":"uBz85KS2YD"}],"key":"urClKJogxJ"}],"key":"gVeM0upgB8"}],"key":"zwkBDr3XoJ"}],"key":"qFSxYvt5Zo"}],"key":"cb6nUMCfLD"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":117,"column":1},"end":{"line":117,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rationale and alternatives","position":{"start":{"line":117,"column":1},"end":{"line":117,"column":1}},"key":"XHegLqH68Z"}],"identifier":"rationale-and-alternatives","label":"Rationale and alternatives","html_id":"rationale-and-alternatives","implicit":true,"key":"t7kP44vT3O"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":127,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A previous (stale) JEP proposed to integrate LSP and to adopt Monaco editor, which would entail\nbringing a heavy dependency and large reliance on continuous development of Monaco by Microsoft; it\nwas not clear whether Monaco would allow efficient use in multi-editor notebook setting and the work\non the integration stalled a few years ago. Differently to that previous proposal we ","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"uY7PmbBxEy"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"do not","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"wqNEdtIpWg"}],"key":"sTnghkA6j1"},{"type":"text","value":"\npropose to adopt any specific implementation, yet we bring a working implementation for CodeMirror 5\neditor, which is already in use by two of the official front-ends for Jupyter (Jupyter Notebook and\nJupyterLab). While the nearly-feature-complete CodeMirror 6 has specifically declared LSP\nintegration to be a non-goal, it does however provide a number of features which would allow for\ncleaner integration of multiple sources of editor annotation, such as named bundles of marks.","position":{"start":{"line":119,"column":1},"end":{"line":119,"column":1}},"key":"mPQvuDb39m"}],"key":"YAJREaWZtc"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":129,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Jupyter originally driving innovation in the field is now in some communities perceived as a\ndriver behind bad coding practices due to the lack of available toolset in the official frontends.\nAlternative formats to ipynb were proposed and sometimes the only motivation was a better\nIDE-features support.","position":{"start":{"line":129,"column":1},"end":{"line":129,"column":1}},"key":"jEbN4N44Ds"}],"key":"UNtGJE3EEW"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prior art","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"key":"lCpxtaRR4L"}],"identifier":"prior-art","label":"Prior art","html_id":"prior-art","implicit":true,"key":"qldxKZUjE6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":140,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multiple editors already support the Language Server Protocol, whether directly or via extension\npoints, including VSCode, Atom, Brackets (Adobe), Spyder, Visual Studio and many more. The list of\nclients and their capabilities is described at the community-maintained\n","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"C2edu1DBap"},{"type":"link","url":"https://langserver.org/","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"knowledge site","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"mWE7HNO97H"}],"urlSource":"https://langserver.org/","key":"p7tAQaVe7q"},{"type":"text","value":" in the “LSP clients” section and at official website of\nthe ","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"hG9lAUotpj"},{"type":"link","url":"https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/implementors/tools/","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"LSP protocol","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"XYosfztsnB"}],"urlSource":"https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/implementors/tools/","key":"GXapaO9j4Z"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"p7eBI5pcBZ"}],"key":"yU0g14lGxq"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":142,"column":1},"end":{"line":145,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multiple proprietary notebook interfaces attempted integration of language features such as those\nprovided by LSP, including Google Colab, Datalore, Deepnote, and Polynote; due to proprietary\nimplementation details it is not clear how many of the existing solutions employ LSP (or its subset)\nunder the hood.","position":{"start":{"line":142,"column":1},"end":{"line":142,"column":1}},"key":"Uerchx0H